    "created_at": "2015-06-09T07:58:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-06-09T07:58:43Z",
    "body": "Actually `ProgressEvent` is exposed only on `Window` in Blink, but I believe that's an oversight. I think the spec should expose all the interfaces in the same contexts and Blink should change.\n\nTo me, throwing `InvalidAccessError` when sync XHR is attempted in any non-whitelisted context sounds pretty good. Which kinds of workers already depend on sync XHR I don't know, but we could measure it.\n\n@coonsta and @jakearchibald, thoughts?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
