    "created_at": "2022-09-12T02:02:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-12T02:02:28Z",
    "body": "> Well, we also want folks to move to `fetch()`. That started in 2015 and is especially true today.\r\n\r\nfetch() eventually added an abort, but you still have to cobble together your own timeout.  And the abort is quite a bit clunkier than what it takes for an XHR.  I hope in the future you'll make sure your API's are a superset (and preferably cleaner) before forcing the sunset of old API's.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
